         <COLUMN NAME="SCNRO_NM" TYPE="CHAR" PK="NO"  NULL="NO">(FR/AC) Externally Matched Names</COLUMN>
         <COLUMN NAME="SCNRO_TX" TYPE="CHAR" PK="NO"  NULL="NO">Financial institutions regularly scan their Accounts/Customer files against watch lists as part of their due diligence process to ensure they know their customers and have limited their exposure to the risk of fraud. Entities are considered high risk based on their presence on a public (governmental or quasi-governmental), third party repositories which flag known or suspected fraudsters, or private (internal) watch lists, such as those of known fraud suspects or perpetrators. Several Mantas clients use third party platforms to identify potentially risky entities based on fuzzy name matching.
The objective of this scenario is to generate an alert for each matched record (customer/account name match). This provides a single repository for the alerts to facilitate analysis and include the information in an entity's alert history so that these matches might be considered in prior match counts in the scoring of future alerts and for audit purposes, enabling closer scrutiny of the customer or account activities, as well as flagging for possible closure.</COLUMN>
